## SQ-PFS-01
@group A, plus the jar in `srv/mods` and `-Dcdevperfbot.out=perf/bot` in `user_jvm_args.txt`
@commands Boot; `pbot status`; `pbot spawn bot1 ~ ~ ~`; `pbot list`; `forge tps`; grep latest.log for `bot1` and `Exception`
@pass `cdevperfbot ok`; a normal join line, no exception from Forge networking, FTB, KubeJS login handlers or Lightman's; bot listed
@fails NPE in a mod's login handler: that mod reads something `BotConnection` lacks (remote address, channel attribute); stack names it
@reviewed 2026-11-20
> pbot status
> pbot spawn bot1 3000 -60 3000 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot list
> forge tps
expect cdevperfbot ok
expect bot1 joined the game
expect bot1
reject Exception|\tat
look the join line is a normal one; no stack from Forge networking, FTB, KubeJS login handlers or Lightman's in the row log
## SQ-PFS-02
@group A, `gamerule randomTickSpeed 3`
@commands `fill` a 9 x 9 farmland + `wheat[age=0]` patch 10 blocks from spawn; `pbot spawn bot1` beside it; 5 min; `execute if block` count of age > 0; repeat with the bot removed
@pass Wheat grows with the bot, none without
@fails No growth: `BotPlayer.tick` chunk move not running, or the bot is in spectator
@reviewed 2026-11-20
# tickwarp replaces the 5 min (6000 ticks); the second field is forceloaded without a player, so it gets no random ticks
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> fill 2995 -61 3005 3003 -61 3013 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
> fill 2995 -60 3005 3003 -60 3013 minecraft:wheat[age=0]
> cdevtest tickwarp 6000
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=6000 600
> cdevtest ages 2995 -60 3005 3003 -60 3013 minecraft:wheat
> forceload add 2995 3005 3003 3013
> pbot remove bot1
> fill 2995 -60 3005 3003 -60 3013 minecraft:wheat[age=0]
> cdevtest tickwarp 6001
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=6001 600
> cdevtest ages 2995 -60 3005 3003 -60 3013 minecraft:wheat
> forceload remove 2995 3005 3003 3013
> pbot spawn bot1 3000 -60 3000 minecraft:overworld survival
expect verb=ages .*n=81 mean=([1-9]|0\.[1-9]|0\.0[1-9])
expect verb=ages .*n=81 mean=0\.000 hist=0:81
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look first verb=ages line (bot beside the field) grew, second (no player) stayed at 0; a second line with growth = a player near 3000 3000 (other rows' bots)
## SQ-PFS-03
@group A
@commands `pbot path bot1 <x+500> 200 <z> 1.5`; after 20 s grep `perf/bot/ticks-*.csv` for `path_done:bot1`; status lines' chunk column; `pbot census t`
@pass `path_done` after about 334 ticks; loaded chunks follow; `perf/bot/census-t.json` written
@fails Chunks don't follow: `ServerChunkCache.move` not reached
@reviewed 2026-11-26
# the path is 500 blocks at 1.5 b/t (about 334 ticks): a 400-tick warp replaces the 20 s
# bot1 spawned here too so the row reruns alone (judge-7, r1120nv, 2026-11-21)
> execute unless entity bot1 run pbot spawn bot1 3000 -60 3000 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> pbot path bot1 3500 200 3000 1.5
> cdevtest tickwarp 400
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=400 120
> cdevtest player bot1
> pbot census t
shell grep -l "path_done:bot1" perf/bot/ticks-*.csv
shell test -s perf/bot/census-t.json
expect census t entities \d+ block_entities \d+
expect verb=player name=bot1 .*x=3(4[89]\d|500)[. ]
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look the status lines' chunk column follows the bot (perf/bot/ticks-*.csv); path_done near tick 334 of the path
## SQ-PFS-04
@group A
@commands `kill -9` the scratch JVM (recorded pid only); `tail -2` of the tick file; `jfr assemble srv/perf/jfr-repo/<dir> x.jfr`
@pass Complete lines to the last second; assemble works
@fails
@draft kills the scratch JVM with kill -9 on purpose: that ends any qrun batch (the crash watch reports CRASH); run it by hand after the last row of a run
## SQ-PFS-05
@group suite S and N
@commands `setsid nohup python3 tools/perf/suite/perf_suite.py run general g1 > /dev/null 2>&1 &` (about 2 h 15 min); then `perf_suite.py report g1`
@pass Every G row `ok` or a triaged ending in `perf/suite/g1/*/endings/`; G02 about 5-6 ms (perf.md 12.1); record the summary in perf_suite.md
@fails Read `runner.log`; `resume g1` after fixing
@draft perf suite run (`perf_suite.py run general g1`, about 2 h 15 min, its own boots and bots), not a qrun batch; no /cdevtest readback replaces it
